      "text": "The bug is that `job.get_unitary()` has no unitary to return. Aer only saves the unitary when the circuit contains a `save_unitary` instruction, and the circuit has none. Adding `circuit.save_unitary()` after the Hadamard fixes this.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumRegister, ClassicalRegister, QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit_aer import AerSimulator\n\nqreg_q = QuantumRegister(1, 'q')\ncreg_c = ClassicalRegister(1, 'c')\ncircuit = QuantumCircuit(qreg_q, creg_c)\ncircuit.h(0)\n# FIX: No save instruction in circuit so Aer never stores the unitary -> added circuit.save_unitary() after the gates, because the unitary simulator only saves the unitary when the circuit contains this instruction\ncircuit.save_unitary()\n\nbackend = AerSimulator(method='unitary')\njob = backend.run(circuit).result()\n\nunitary = job.get_unitary()\nprint(unitary)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
